        # Priority queues for people waiting to enter or exit
        # We store just the index since arrival is non-decreasing and we process in order of arrival for same time
        # However, to be safe with the rule "smallest index goes first", we push (index, arrival_time)
        # Actually, since arrival is sorted, if we push indices, the heap will naturally order by index if times are equal?
        # No, arrival[i] might be same. The problem says "If multiple persons want to go in the same direction, the person with the smallest index goes first."
        # Since we iterate i from 0 to n-1, if we push into heap, the heap will order by (index, arrival_time).
        # But wait, arrival is non-decreasing. So if arrival[i] == arrival[j] with i < j, then (i, arrival[i]) < (j, arrival[j]).
        # So storing (index, arrival_time) works perfectly.

        enter_queue = []  # (index, arrival_time)
        exit_queue = []   # (index, arrival_time)

